{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/914928-supernatural-creature-based-scales","id":914928,"title":"Supernatural Creature Based Scales","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-06-15T11:12:14-07:00","id":914928,"title":"Supernatural Creature Based Scales","content":"I had a thought reading in a the Mage forum and thought I would share it in hope of sparking other people's imaginations too.<div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><b>Scale</b>: Blood of Magi<br /> <b>Prerequisite:</b> Siphon the Soul<br /> The vampire injects a Mage with a hallucinogenic and toxic alchemical mixture that includes his Vitae, the vampire must then be completely devoid of Vitae not gained from this procedure, and bite and drain the mage to death.<br /> While the vampire only has the Vitae gained through this procedure, he has Peripheral Mage\u2019s Sight of the Ruling Arcanums any Mages fed upon in this manner. While the vampire has the peripheral mage\u2019s sight, he may use Active Mage Sight, or Scrutinize as a Mage by spending 1 Vitae and 1 Willpower.<br /> Should a vampire gain Vitae from any other source than use of this Scale, the abilities of this Scale are lost and it must be reenacted anew.</div>I would also appreciate feedback, as well as Scales you all can think up.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":3279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","user":"Pale_Crusader","date":". 06-15-2016, 06:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-15T11:32:34-07:00","id":914940,"title":"","content":"I like the requirement of being free of Vitae and having to drain all of the mage's blood and the ability lasting while it has the mage's blood. But I feel like Mage Sight is for the most part worthless to a vampire. Perhaps offering something like a proximus of the victim's Path, with blessings based on the mage's rotes but amount capped by Blood Potency? It does make the ability more powerful but it is still limited by the mana.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 06-15-2016, 02:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-15T12:07:36-07:00","id":914965,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/914928-supernatural-creature-based-scales?p=914940#post914940\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I feel like Mage Sight is for the most part worthless to a vampire.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Are you familiar with Scrutinizing to resolve Mysteries? <i>Mage: The Awakening 2E </i>Page 92<br /> <br /> It is amazingly powerful and just plain better than most other investigation/information-gaining type powers. It has the capacity of revealing Truth (Capital 'T') about anything focused upon.<br /> <br /> Also just the Peripheral Mage Sight allows detecting powers in use unless the power used is supernaturally cloaked somehow automatically and Active Mage Sight allows detecting a whole lot more.<br /> <br /> Vampires with the ability to pierce the petty and grand deceptions of the Dance Macabre would be a fearsome threat, and this ability could be tempting enough to get vampires to start a war with mages, in my opinion. Imagine having your whole grand scheme reduced to an abstract Opacity score for a Mystery that can be seen through by someone gaining successes by Scrutinizing with Mage Sight. Also you don't even need to be present, the user of mage sight merely needs someone, something, or someplace part of the plan.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":3279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","user":"Pale_Crusader","date":". 06-15-2016, 03:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-15T13:00:22-07:00","id":915008,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pale_Crusader</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/914928-supernatural-creature-based-scales?p=914965#post914965\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are you familiar with Scrutinizing to resolve Mysteries? <i>Mage: The Awakening 2E </i>Page 92<br /> <br /> It is amazingly powerful and just plain better than most other investigation/information-gaining type powers. It has the capacity of revealing Truth (Capital 'T') about anything focused upon.<br /> <br /> Also just the Peripheral Mage Sight allows detecting powers in use unless the power used is supernaturally cloaked somehow automatically and Active Mage Sight allows detecting a whole lot more.<br /> <br /> Vampires with the ability to pierce the petty and grand deceptions of the Dance Macabre would be a fearsome threat, and this ability could be tempting enough to get vampires to start a war with mages, in my opinion. Imagine having your whole grand scheme reduced to an abstract Opacity score for a Mystery that can be seen through by someone gaining successes by Scrutinizing with Mage Sight. Also you don't even need to be present, the user of mage sight merely needs someone, something, or someplace part of the plan.</div> </div> </div> </div>Without the Arcanum, Peripheral Mage Sight is Unseen Senses that only works for active effects. Active Sight is useful if you have the right Arcanum. But Scrutinizing it is very limited. 'Any magical puzzle, any lingering spell, any otherworldly enigma is potentially a Mystery.' Which is great, except the soap opera that is the court is not a magical puzzle, lingering spell or otherworldly enigma. I haven't been keeping up with the FAQ-gathering, but it really seems like Mage Sight, at least the scrutinize and revelation aspects, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/842927-range-of-mage-peripheral-sight?p=854402#post854402\">deals with the magical nature of things, not the mundane.</a><br /> <br /> Then of course, you also have Auspex 2 or 3 able to do the same thing, arguably better, without requiring a Humanity Breaking Point for killing a mage you've somehow previously managed to dose with chemicals..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 06-15-2016, 04:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-15T13:21:56-07:00","id":915029,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/914928-supernatural-creature-based-scales?p=915008#post915008\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Without the Arcanum,</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, I see what I missed putting in the write up that I intended. I will edit the original post. I'll post the original form here so people understand your criticism.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Original Post Version</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Scale</b>: Blood of Magi<br /> <b>Prerequisite:</b> Beast\u2019s Hunger<br /> The vampire injects a Mage with a hallucinogenic and toxic alchemical mixture that includes his Vitae, the vampire must then be completely devoid of Vitae not gained from this procedure, and bite and drain the mage to death.<br /> While the vampire only has the Vitae gained through this procedure, he has Peripheral Mage\u2019s Sight of any Mages fed upon in this manner. While the vampire has the peripheral mage\u2019s sight, he may use Active Mage Sight, or Scrutinize as a Mage by spending 1 Vitae and 1 Willpower.<br /> Should a vampire gain Vitae from any other source than use of this Scale, the abilities of this Scale are lost and it must be reenacted anew.</div> </div> </div> </div>Edit: the original post is now as I meant the meaning to be. It makes it so a vampire not afraid of committing atrocities could rack up all ten mages sights. Also good quote of rules<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>terpsichordean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/886930-sample-mysteries#post886930\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Any magical puzzle, any lingering spell, any otherworldly enigma is potentially a Mystery. The Storyteller decides on the<br /> particulars of the Mystery, which break down into three parts: Opacity, surface information, and deep information.&quot; (p. 93)<br /> <br /> I'm starting a new game, but need clarity on coming up with specific Mysteries. Every Order has some samples, but they're very open-ended. For Storytellers and Players alike, what Mysteries are you planning to insert in your game? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Vampire politics may or may not fall under &quot;any otherworldly enigma&quot; especially with things like Carthian law and Invitctus Oaths having supernatural affects.<br /> <br /> And Scales are much cheaper than Discipline dots.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":3279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","user":"Pale_Crusader","date":". 06-15-2016, 04:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-15T14:37:12-07:00","id":915089,"title":"","content":"<b>Scale: </b>Deadman's Ashes<br /> <b>Prerequisite:</b> Shed the Beast's Skin<br /> By using the cremains of a Sin-Eater mixed in a poultice of rare herbs and your Vitae, which is smeared on your internal organs through an incision in your abdomen, you gain the Immortal Dread Power for the night. You no longer enter torpor upon having all your health boxes filled with lethal damage, instead you &quot;bleed out&quot; as a mortal would but it takes the form of your body crumbling to ash which fades from existence. After your body has been fully reduced to ash, you entering the next scene of your choice by stepping out of the shadows at or near that scene which includes someone present at or responsible for your last &quot;death&quot;. This Scale is incompatible with using the Blush, and trying to have this Scale and the Blush active at the same time causes the Blush to fail and the vampire to bleed out all remaining Vitae, which is rendered unsuitable for feeding. Should you fail to enter a scene after being reduced to ash before the next dawn, you meet Final Death.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":3279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","user":"Pale_Crusader","date":". 06-15-2016, 06:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-15T14:55:12-07:00","id":915108,"title":"","content":"Sounds like you just have one of the preview Scales of the Ziva Coil. I think it even allows stealing the powers of other supernaturals.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-15T15:50:24-07:00","id":915148,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/914928-supernatural-creature-based-scales?p=915108#post915108\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sounds like you just have one of the preview Scales of the Ziva Coil. I think it even allows stealing the powers of other supernaturals.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Ziva Coil? <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1_J83T-t9g-87pvtUTKCZIJ2QQzCTOzUclkWJjsvb814/edit#heading=h.3tkbuu69w3m6\" target=\"_blank\">*Google Search*</a><br /> <br /> Good call! I agree it makes a better Prerequisite.<br /> <br /> Editing previous posts to reflect your advice.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_c